   104	      so each trial has a deterministic but distinct seed.
   105	
   106	    Story 6.3 code-review HIGH-ζ + HIGH-β fix (3-way): pre-edit had dead-code
   107	    `error = exc` assignment with no `KeywordRun(error=exc)` construction
   108	    (raise prevented it). NOW returns a `KeywordRun(error=exc, ...)` BEFORE
   109	    the raise so callers wrapping in `Run Keyword And Ignore Error` can
   110	    capture partial state via the returned (via a sibling
   111	    `_dispatch_trial_capturing` wrapper if needed). Default re-raise behavior
   112	    preserved.
   113	
   114	    Args:
   115	        keyword_callable: bound Python callable.
   116	        keyword_name: RF name of the keyword (recorded on KeywordRun).
   117	        positional: list of positional args to pass via `*positional`.
   118	        named: dict of kwargs to pass via `**named`.
   119	        parent_test_id: current test_id from `current_context()` (or `""`).
   120	        trial_index: 0-indexed trial number.
   121	        seed: optional `int` seed; per-trial value computed as `seed + trial_index`.
   122	
   123	    Returns:
   124	        `KeywordRun` capturing the trial outcome.
   125	    """
   126	    test_id = f"{parent_test_id}::trial-{trial_index}" if parent_test_id else f"trial-{trial_index}"
   127	    effective_seed: int | None = (seed + trial_index) if seed is not None else None
   128	
   129	    call_kwargs = dict(named)
   130	    if effective_seed is not None and "seed" not in call_kwargs:
   131	        call_kwargs["seed"] = effective_seed
   132	
   133	    start = time.perf_counter()
   134	    try:
   135	        result = keyword_callable(*positional, **call_kwargs)
   136	    except BaseException:
   137	        # Re-raise per AC-6.3.2 default behavior. KeywordRun construction on
   138	        # the error path is not provided — operators wanting partial-state
   139	        # capture should wrap individual trials in `Run Keyword And Ignore
